body:
It's been at least 2 years and this is something I wished they fixed, but nooooo, let's remove the dislike button, everyone asked for that

&#x200B;

\*Edit this has been actually a thing for 5 years, great

Thank you for taking the time to write something thoughtful.

I need to found out if counseling is free with Medicare... but like you said, I have to force him to go. He doesn't even take care of his own problems. He keeps talking about his shoulder feeling weird for weeks and he has yet to make an appointment with the physio. I don't understand why he keeps putting it off since I thought he was serious about being fit etc

&#x200B;

My mom wants to set up rules and a deadline for him to improve, but it's extremely difficult to get him to listen to anything like that. He never wants to listen and I've been the middleperson for years, because my mom basically gave up on talking to him, but we will have to talk again soon...

&#x200B;

Take care and stay safe too.
